---
/**
 * Ships the runnable-examples script, and nothing else.
 *
 * It exists as a component purely so a page can decide not to render it: Astro
 * bundles a component's `<script>` onto the pages that actually use it, so a
 * lesson whose examples are all teaching fragments stays a zero-JavaScript page.
 * Putting the same tag directly in the layout would put the bundle on all 58.
 */
---
<script>
  import '../scripts/runnable.js';
</script>
